    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1277A\n\nSPONSOR: KRUEGER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to providing for online\nand in-person instruction and examination of election inspectors, poll\nclerks and election coordinators\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide for electronic administration of instruction and examinations\nfor election inspectors, poll clerks, and election coordinators and to\nremove the annual course requirement for reappointed election officials\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 3-412 of the election law to provide that\ninstruction and examinations for election inspectors, poll clerks, and\nelection coordinators shall be offered both electronically and in\nperson. Removes the requirement that the course of instruction be taken\nevery year. After taking the course and passing the examination the\nfirst year, election inspectors, poll clerks, and election coordinators\nwill be required to pass the examination on an annual basis, but will\nnot be required to retake the course.\n\nProvides for notice of electronic instruction and examination.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAttracting and retaining qualified election inspectors, poll clerks and\nelection coordinators is a problem for many local boards of election\nacross the state. This legislation modernizes the practices of adminis-\ntering examinations and courses of instruction by providing the opportu-\nnity to complete these requirements online. It also removes that mandate\nthat the course of instruction be taken annually. This will allow expe-\nrienced election officials to demonstrate their competence by completing\nthe exam without repeating a time-consuming course every year.\n\nAllowing an electronic option and changing the course requirement would\nlikely also reduce costs for local boards of elections.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019-20: S.6635/A.8514 Epstein - Died in Committee\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nPotential savings to local boards of elections\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately, amendment or repeal of any rule or\nregulation necessary for the implementation of this law on its effective\ndate are authorized to be made or completed on or before such date.\n",
